.TH GPU-SWITCH 8 "2026-11-22" "gpu-switch" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
gpu-switch \- choose the NVIDIA dGPU power state for the next boot (ASUS laptops)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gpu-switch
.RI [ status ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.br
.B gpu-switch
.BR on | off | toggle
.RB [ \-n ]
.br
.B gpu-switch apply
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gpu-switch
switches the NVIDIA discrete GPU fully on or off through the ASUS firmware
attribute
.IR dgpu_disable .
The change cannot be made safely while the system runs, so
.B gpu-switch
only records the
.I desired
state; it is applied at the next shutdown or reboot by
.BR gpu-switch.service ,
after all user sessions have ended.
.PP
With the dGPU off the laptop uses less power on battery, but every output
wired to the NVIDIA GPU (on the GA401QM: the USB-C/DisplayPort video output,
used by the dock) does not work. The setting lives in firmware, so other
operating systems (Windows "Eco mode") see it too.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the current state and the state after the next reboot (default).
.TP
.BR on ", " off
Set the desired state for the next boot.
.TP
.B toggle
Flip the desired state.
.TP
.B apply
Apply the desired state now. Root only; meant to be run by
.B gpu-switch.service
at shutdown. When switching off, the NVIDIA kernel modules are unloaded
first; if that fails (the GPU is still in use), nothing is changed and the
request stays pending for the next reboot.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-notify
Also show the result as a desktop notification (needs
.BR notify-send ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short usage summary.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/gpu-switch/desired
Desired state,
.B on
or
.BR off .
Writable by group
.BR wheel ,
so no password is needed. If missing, the current state is kept.
.TP
.I /sys/class/firmware-attributes/asus-armoury/attributes/dgpu_disable/current_value
Firmware attribute: 0 = dGPU on, 1 = dGPU off.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/gpu-switch.service
Applies the desired state at shutdown.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B gpu-switch off && sudo reboot
Leave the dock: dGPU off from the next boot on.
.TP
.B gpu-switch on && sudo reboot
Before docking: dGPU on again.
.TP
.B journalctl -b -1 -u gpu-switch
What happened at the last shutdown.
.TP
.B journalctl -u gpu-switch -p warning
Only failed switches, across all boots.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B apply
logs to the journal (via
.BR gpu-switch.service )
with these priorities:
.TP
.B warning
The NVIDIA kernel modules could not be unloaded, so the dGPU was not
switched off. Nothing is broken; the request stays pending and is retried at
the next reboot.
.TP
.B err
The firmware write failed, or the firmware still reports the old state
afterwards. The request stays pending.
.TP
.B info
The switch succeeded, or there was nothing to do.
.PP
After a failed switch,
.B gpu-switch status
still shows a pending change.
.SH NOTES
Do not use
.B asusctl armoury set dgpu_disable
at the same time; it queues its own change that asusd applies at shutdown,
and that path doesn't wait for user sessions to end.
.PP
In sway,
.B $mod+Shift+g
runs
.BR "gpu-switch toggle \-\-notify" .
.SH UNINSTALL
.nf
sudo systemctl disable --now gpu-switch.service
sudo rm /etc/systemd/system/gpu-switch.service /usr/local/bin/gpu-switch \e
        /usr/local/share/man/man8/gpu-switch.8
sudo rm -r /var/lib/gpu-switch
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asusctl (1),
.BR systemd.unit (5)
